2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1063) 'STE enforcement moves to the plugin
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1063) 'Delete `scripts/ste-lint-decisions.py`. Delete its `npm run lint:ste` entry in `thirdparty/3d_studio/package.json`. Delete its step in `scripts/ci.sh`, and its hook in `.pre-commit-config.yaml`. STE enforcement now runs once, in the plugin's `Stop` hook, at write time.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1063) 'See `DETAILS.md` for what moved to the plugin, including three new checks this repository contributed upstream. It also names what the deleted script's aggregate score this repository does not gain back.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1063) 'RFD66606-1000 named the deleted script. RFD66606-1059 wired `npm run lint:ste` into `scripts/ci.sh`. This RFD removes that step, and nothing replaces it. `fire/claude-ste-plugin#1` is the PR that carries this repository's contribution upstream.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1063) 'Why the plugin checks earlier
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1063) '`fire/claude-ste-plugin` is a Claude Code plugin. It checks at a better point in the process. It lints the reply before the reply reaches a file, and it asks for a rewrite. The old script caught a violation only after a commit already held it. Two enforcement points for one rule is the DRY policy's own complaint, turned on this repository's own tooling.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1063) 'What moved where
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-1063) 'Several checks the deleted script hand-wrote already existed in the plugin, and more precisely. The plugin cites an ASD-STE100 Part 1 rule number for each one. Its sentence splitter and word counter follow CommonMark structure, not a line-based heuristic.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-1063) 'Three checks were new. Each one went upstream instead of staying local, in `fire/claude-ste-plugin#1`:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-1063) '- `style.bloat`, for an inflated word such as "utilize"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-1063) '- `style.marketing`, for a marketing word such as "seamless"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-1063) '- `style.dash`, for an em dash that joins two clauses
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-1063) 'This repository's own `decisions/` tree is the prose the PR tested them against. The plugin checks all three now, in every project it installs into, not only this one.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-1063) 'What this repository does not gain back
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-1063) 'The deleted script scored a whole document, at violations per 100 words. It also read many files at once and printed one pass or fail line per file. The plugin has no equivalent to either. It reports one finding per line, for one file at a time, and it does not score a document as a whole. A CI run that wants one pass/fail number across every RFD does not have that number anymore.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-1063) 'This RFD accepts that loss. `decisions/README.md`'s STE policy never asked for a score. It asked for STE prose. The `Stop` hook catches a violation earlier than a CI gate can, on every reply that touches this repository, not only on a push.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-1063) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-1063) 'RFD66606-1000 named `scripts/ste-lint-decisions.py` as this repository's STE linter. It scored each RFD's prose at violations per 100 words. It ran in CI, through `npm run lint:ste`. It ran again in `.pre-commit-config.yaml`'s `ste-lint` hook.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1063  1 LINE
 Text:Written
